Content upgrade: use a snapshot of the hooks supplied by the versioned loader.
The snapshot copies the major and minor maps down to the hook functions,
unwrapped from { contentUpgrade }, so a later script cannot change earlier
hooks, even by editing the registry in place. Explicit undefined snapshots
prevent libraries without an upgrades script from borrowing another version's
hooks. Retain the global fallback for upstream loaders.

